535
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:25,343
Okay, shoot.

536
00:22:25,385 --> 00:22:27,305
Okay.

537
00:22:27,345 --> 00:22:29,807
Um, all right, here's the deal.

538
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:32,310
Oh, no!

539
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:34,145
What, what is it?

540
00:22:34,187 --> 00:22:38,274
Oh, major shampoo explosion.

541
00:22:38,316 --> 00:22:39,608
All right, look.

542
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:41,902
Uh, look, Ross,
this really isn't easy.

543
00:22:41,944 --> 00:22:43,988
Oh, it's all over everything!

544
00:22:46,573 --> 00:22:48,868
Why? Why me?

545
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:52,872
Because you took
300 bottles of shampoo?

546
00:22:54,332 --> 00:22:56,667
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
You were saying?

547
00:22:56,709 --> 00:22:58,376
Well, yeah, okay, look.

548
00:22:58,418 --> 00:22:59,628
It's about me and...

549
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:02,215
Oh, not another one!

550
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:06,426
Oh, my... and this moisturizer.

551
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:08,428
It's even harder to clean!

552
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:13,726
Why? Why do bad things
happen to good people?

553
00:23:15,728 --> 00:23:17,355
Wow.

554
00:23:17,395 --> 00:23:18,856
Well, clearly
this is not a good time.

555
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:20,233
Uh, you think?!

556
00:23:24,070 --> 00:23:25,696
Okay, bye.

557
00:23:25,738 --> 00:23:28,490
All right, so Mike's
on his way over.

558
00:23:28,532 --> 00:23:30,701
See, you thought you guys
were meeting here

559
00:23:30,743 --> 00:23:33,495
and he thought you were meeting
at the restaurant, so, you know,

560
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:35,622
doesn't really matter
who's right or wrong.

561
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:38,084
The point is...
I'm going to take off.

562
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:39,626
Wait, no.

563
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:40,878
I'm not letting you leave

564
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,629
until you tell me
what's going on here.

565
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:45,841
I mean, are you guys getting
back together or something?

566
00:23:47,093 --> 00:23:48,344
All right.

567
00:23:51,013 --> 00:23:52,681
Susie...
can I call you Susie?

568
00:23:54,392 --> 00:23:56,269
My name is Precious.

569
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:59,313
I can't say that.

570
00:23:59,355 --> 00:24:02,524
Um, Susie, I'm going to be
straight with you.

571
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,903
Mike and I are back together,

572
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:09,531
and, um, unfortunately
that effectively ends

573
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:12,618
your relationship
with him,

574
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:15,037
and he's very sorry about that

575
00:24:15,079 --> 00:24:19,750
and wishes you the best of luck
in all your endeavors.

576
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:21,043
I just can't believe this.

577
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:23,461
Why?

578
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:25,131
Well, I don't...
Why would
he do this?

579
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:27,049
I mean, what's
wrong with me?

580
00:24:27,091 --> 00:24:28,592
Nothing, there's
nothing wrong with you.

581
00:24:28,634 --> 00:24:30,844
I mean, what the hell
am I supposed to do now?

582
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:33,847
Damn it, woman, pull
yourself together.

583
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:37,559
Have some pride,
for the love of God!

584
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:41,730
( crying )

585
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:45,067
Okay, not a fan
of the tough love.

586
00:24:45,109 --> 00:24:46,402
I just can't believe

587
00:24:46,444 --> 00:24:48,904
that Mike didn't
give me any warning.

588
00:24:48,946 --> 00:24:50,823
But he didn't really
know, you know?

589
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:53,075
He wasn't planning
on coming to Barbados

590
00:24:53,117 --> 00:24:54,285
and proposing to me.

591
00:24:54,327 --> 00:24:56,329
He proposed to you?

592
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:59,123
This is the worst birthday ever.

593
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:06,964
Look... Precious.

594
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:10,843
Mike's not worth this.

595
00:25:10,884 --> 00:25:13,095
You're an attractive,
intelligent woman,

596
00:25:13,137 --> 00:25:15,639
and let's face it,
Mike's kind of a wang.

597
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:19,852
And he proposed
to me while he was
still seeing you.

598
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:22,896
He was going to break up
with you on your birthday?

599
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,107
And-- I don't like
to kiss and tell--

600
00:25:25,149 --> 00:25:27,776
but he cheated on you
a lot this weekend.

601
00:25:27,818 --> 00:25:29,945
Oh, my God, you know,
maybe you're right.

602
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:31,238
Maybe I don't need him.

603
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:33,657
I deserve to be treated
with respect.

604
00:25:35,326 --> 00:25:36,618
Screw you, Mike.

605
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,287
You're a coward
and a bastard,

606
00:25:38,329 --> 00:25:39,788
and I hope
you rot in hell.

607
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:47,505
You're welcome.

608
00:25:53,551 --> 00:25:55,137
Honey, you've been in there
for a long time.

609
00:25:55,179 --> 00:25:56,805
Is everything okay?

610
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:58,849
Not really.

611
00:26:01,394 --> 00:26:03,561
I have a problem.

612
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:04,855
Really?

613
00:26:04,897 --> 00:26:07,316
What happened?

614
00:26:07,358 --> 00:26:11,778
Well, I was dancing around
and singing "No Woman, No Cry,"

615
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:16,492
and, uh... I got stuck.

616
00:26:17,535 --> 00:26:18,827
You can't move
at all?

617
00:26:18,869 --> 00:26:21,163
Oh, I can move.

618
00:26:26,544 --> 00:26:30,172
If I untangle you, will you
please get rid of the corn rows?

619
00:26:30,214 --> 00:26:31,798
I guess so.

620
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:35,677
Some of these
look a little frayed.

621
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:38,680
Yeah, I tried
to gnaw myself free.

622
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:43,018
Hey.

623
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:44,144
Hi.

624
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,355
So, did you, uh,
did you tell Ross?

625
00:26:46,397 --> 00:26:47,773
Well, I tried,

626
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:50,776
but then he had
a shampoo-related emergency.

627
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:53,611
So I guess
now it's your turn again.

628
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:55,155
No, no, no,
no, no, no, no.

629
00:26:55,197 --> 00:26:56,532
I think it's better if
you tell him, you know?

630
00:26:56,574 --> 00:26:58,158
And it's easier
for a woman.

631
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,369
That way if he gets mad,
all you have to do is go,

632
00:27:00,411 --> 00:27:04,039
"I didn't mean it.

633
00:27:04,081 --> 00:27:07,084
I'm so sorry."

634
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:12,798
Yeah, 'cause that's what we do.

635
00:27:12,839 --> 00:27:14,300
All right,
all right, okay.

636
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:15,884
Um, how about this,
how about this.

637
00:27:15,926 --> 00:27:17,677
Tomorrow...
Mm-hmm.

638
00:27:17,719 --> 00:27:21,639
Tomorrow we'll both go
and we'll tell him together.

639
00:27:21,681 --> 00:27:24,017
Okay,
that sounds fair.

640
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:24,977
That just means
though...

641
00:27:25,018 --> 00:27:26,979
I know, I know.

642
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,105
But that's okay.

643
00:27:28,147 --> 00:27:29,982
I mean, we can
control ourselves.

644
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:31,024
We're not animals.

645
00:27:31,066 --> 00:27:32,276
( scoffs ):
No.

646
00:27:32,318 --> 00:27:34,111
Of course,
we can wait.

647
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:37,864
All right, so I guess
that means good night then.

648
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:40,242
Yep. Good night.

649
00:27:47,124 --> 00:27:49,876
Good night.

650
00:27:51,128 --> 00:27:52,463
Good night.

651
00:27:59,261 --> 00:28:00,346
Seriously, good night.

652
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:01,096
Stop saying good night.

653
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:02,389
Okay.

654
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:25,996
I'm so sorry.

655
00:28:32,628 --> 00:28:34,963
Look what I found in the drawer.

656
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:40,093
And you said I'd
never wear this.

657
00:28:40,135 --> 00:28:42,262
Now that I untangled you,

658
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:44,598
how about you do
a little something for me?

659
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,559
Sure. What do you have in mind?

660
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,310
I think you know.

661
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,478
Really?

662
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:51,397
I don't really
feel like it.

663
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:53,940
This is what I want to do.

664
00:28:54,983 --> 00:28:56,193
Okay.

665
00:28:56,235 --> 00:28:58,987
I just don't get why
you like it so much.

666
00:29:00,239 --> 00:29:04,451
She's an FBI agent
posing as a beauty contestant.

667
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:06,537
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

